            <ArticleTitle>[Analysis of related factors of tonsil postoperative pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>137-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To explore the related factors of tonsil postoperative pain.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">After founding databank a statistic analysis was performed on 90 cases with tonsillectomy who admitted in our hospital. Chi-square test were used to investigate the related factors for postoperative pain in those patients.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULT" NlmCategory="RESULTS">After Chi-square test, the important effect factors in the postoperative pain were gender, age, surgical methods, preemptive analgesia, physical analgesia and preoperative anxiety level.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The pain after tonsillectomy is influenced by not only surgery itself, but also by preemptive analgesia, preoperative anxiety level and so on.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
